{"Adding a new abstract method `int order()` to the public `CryptoProvider` interface is a binary-incompatible change that will cause `AbstractMethodError` at runtime for any existing third-party implementations not updated in this PR": 0.9426797032356262, "CryptoIntegration.init called with AuthzClient's classloader may cause ServiceLoader to find only the Authz-client-local provider and not providers available via parent or application classloaders": 0.6565215587615967, "CryptoIntegration.init stores the chosen provider in a static volatile singleton that is never changed, so if invoked early with narrow classloader visibility, the system will be locked to that provider even if a more capable provider is available later": 0.7601756453514099, "ASN1Decoder.readLength() returns -1 for indefinite-length encoding, which can make computed length negative when passed to read(int), causing NegativeArraySizeException or crash from new byte[length] without negativity check": 0.9267196655273438, "Crafted DER/ASN.1 input with indefinite-length encodings or malformed lengths can trigger exceptions during parsing and crash the client or consume resources (DoS)": 0.6814777851104736, "AuthzClientCryptoProvider is registered as a CryptoProvider via META-INF/services but most of its methods throw UnsupportedOperationException, which would break any caller relying on those capabilities": 0.5283337831497192, "ServiceLoader provider selection now silently prefers highest 'order' provider, allowing an attacker or misconfiguration to place a CryptoProvider with higher order value that will be preferred automatically and used globally": 0.41746675968170166, "Malicious crypto provider selection is silent (ignored providers only logged at DEBUG), so operators may not notice a non-default provider is being used": 0.4640791416168213}